Subject: hyper-rt from kiln's own runtime, crates/kiln-rt
Why: kiln's runtime is its own copy of hyper-rt (crates/kiln-rt/ORIGIN.md), which every crate kiln builds that names hyper-rt takes. Mantle's crates take it by path, which a patch can't reach, and two path packages named hyper-rt 0.1.0 can't share a lock file, so each path points at kiln's copy, as hyper-raft's own crates' do (vendor/hyper-raft/UPSTREAM.md). Cargo.lock doesn't say where a path package lives, so it is unchanged

diff --git a/crates/chunk/Cargo.toml b/crates/chunk/Cargo.toml
index dbb12e20af6f98150058f8eba6420b3f48bea118..71429efbc2368b4878f8b36d774331aabdf964bf 100644
--- a/crates/chunk/Cargo.toml
+++ b/crates/chunk/Cargo.toml
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@ hyper-block = { path = "../../../hyper-raft/crates/hyper-block", features = ["si
 # The index's bytes a fragment, counted by its allocator (tests/index_memory.rs).
 hyper-measure = { path = "../../../hyper-raft/crates/hyper-measure" }
 # The runtime a `Reader`'s owner runs on, for its tests (tests/reader.rs).
-hyper-rt = { path = "../../../hyper-raft/crates/hyper-rt" }
+hyper-rt = { path = "../../../../crates/kiln-rt" }
 proptest.workspace = true
 tempfile.workspace = true
 
